                <person xml:id="PIN04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John Pretor - and sons</forename>
                        <surname>Pinney</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1740">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1818"/>
                    <occupation>Merchant and Planter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope notes:The last entry 23.3.1802 Sup at Davy's with Pinney ser.,
                            was probably John Pretor Pinney DNB 1740-1818, the others probably either him or one
                            of his sons John Frederick or Azariah.
                            William Wordsworth (see DNB 1770-1850) and his sister were tenants of
                            Pinney in Somerset 1795-7. Basil Montagu is said to have introduced
                            them. A very close study of Wordsworth's letters might establish which
                            of the brothers and father appeared in Godwin's diary.
                        See ODNB.</p>
                    </note>
